{
  "description": "Type the 403s the service operations answer for a feature the organization's plan or settings do not include: GET and POST .../jwtProviders, PUT and DELETE .../jwtProviders/{name}: {\"status\": 403, \"error\": \"FORBIDDEN: Cannot use JWT authentication providers in SCALE pricing package\"} (get by name 757cc0d9-26b4-40ad-ad16-6086367c9b52, list 6e7d7036-e65c-428b-8eec-269a6d5d8122, create ad6f643b-5312-417a-b03b-14324410a734); GET and PATCH .../clickhouseSettings, GET .../clickhouseSettings/schema, GET and DELETE .../clickhouseSettings/{settingName}: \"FORBIDDEN: ClickHouse settings API is not enabled for this organization. Please contact support to enable this feature\" (update 4b53bb2b-ff97-4638-849b-7d6120c306fa); GET and PATCH .../replicaAwareRouting: \"FORBIDDEN: early access API endpoint\" (update dda6edb8-7251-4d0d-8b3c-fe149714225a); PUT .../upgradeWindow: \"FORBIDDEN: Cannot use scheduled upgrades in SCALE pricing package\" (dec211d0-e105-443e-821c-e817b38773e8). The spec types them only as the shared envelope, so they surfaced as the generic Forbidden, which is also what a missing permission answers. Observed live 2026-11-12 on a SCALE-package organization. The scaling schedule, replica scaling (horizontal autoscaling), backup configuration and backup bucket operations are not gated there and carry no error.",
  "patches": [
    {
